    <title>Auditing UK energy policy without a cluster</title>
    <link href="https://endjin.com/what-we-think/talks/auditing-uk-energy-policy-without-a-cluster" rel="alternate"/>
    <link href="https://endjin.com/what-we-think/talks/auditing-uk-energy-policy-without-a-cluster/replies.atom" rel="replies" type="application/atom+xml" thr:count="15" thr:updated="2026-06-30T14:00:00Z"/>
    <id>urn:uuid:1225c695-cfb8-4ebb-aaaa-80da344efa6c</id>
    <published>2026-06-29T05:30:00Z</published>
    <updated>2026-06-29T06:00:00Z</updated>
    <summary>A laptop, a duck, and twenty years of wind: auditing UK energy policy with DuckDB.</summary>

    <!-- Threading extension -->
    <thr:total>15</thr:total>

    <content type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>Barry Smart audits twenty years of fragmented government energy data on a <strong>single laptop</strong>.</p>
        <p>What replaced the monolithic warehouse:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Python ingestion guarded by strict data contracts</li>
          <li>Parquet and a DuckDB medallion model</li>
          <li>Requirements written in Gherkin as composable, tested functions</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </content>

    <app:control>
      <app:draft>no</app:draft>
    </app:control>

